  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 103 AM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nThe long term forecast will be characterized by much colder\ntemperatures compared to the well above-average conditions of\nlate. The signal from global ensembles and the NBM is clear;\ndaily high temperatures will drop into the 40s to low 50s, while\novernight lows will plummet into the 20s. In fact, NBM QMD data\nare depicting medium to high probabilities (50-90%) of \ntemperatures dropping into the teens across the eastern Ozarks \nby mid-week. Indeed, Thanksgiving morning appears it will be \nquite cold with temperatures in the teens and 20s across the\nentire forecast area. \n\nEnsemble cluster analysis shows typical model divergence and\nforecast uncertainty by the middle of the week, though a slight\nplurality of members suggests some precipitation chances return \nby Friday. At this point, NBM PoPs remain less than 20% for \nsouthwest Missouri and southeast Kansas through the long term \nforecast period.",
